    <h3>A Family Farm in the Smoky Mountains</h3>

    <p>
      Smoky Mountain Acres began in 2025 when our family started raising animals and building a working farm in the mountains of East Tennessee. Located near Cosby, Tennessee, Cosby Campground, and Great Smoky Mountains National Park, our farm gives visitors a chance to experience farm life away from the busier tourist areas around Gatlinburg and the Smokies.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <i class="bi bi-check2-all"></i>
        <span>Home to Kune Kune pigs, Red Wattle pigs, Katahdin sheep, chickens, and other farm animals.</span>
      </li>

      <li>
        <i class="bi bi-check2-all"></i>
        <span>Family-friendly farm tours with opportunities to meet, pet, and feed animals while learning how a small working farm operates.</span>
      </li>

      <li>
        <i class="bi bi-check2-all"></i>
        <span>Focused on responsible livestock care, pasture-based management, rotational grazing, and practical modern homesteading.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Visitors come to Smoky Mountain Acres for a quieter, more hands-on experience in the Smoky Mountains. Our farm tours are designed for families, children, homesteaders, and travelers looking for things to do near Cosby and Great Smoky Mountains National Park.
    </p>

    <p>
      We also periodically offer livestock and farm products for sale, including Kune Kune and Red Wattle pigs for pets, homesteads, breeding, or whole-hog meat purchases, along with Katahdin sheep, chickens, and farm-fresh eggs. Availability changes throughout the year as our farm continues to grow.
    </p>

    <p>
      Our goal is to build a productive, welcoming family farm that combines modern livestock management with the character of life in the Smoky Mountains. Whether you are visiting the area, looking for farm animals, or simply want to show your children where food and farm life come from, Smoky Mountain Acres offers a small-farm experience rooted in the mountains we call home.
    </p>

